      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is a bit strange to have a dexpreopt test in the apex dir. Is it because you need access to apex package internals somewhere? These factory functions seems to be accessible from the outside though.\n\nThe apex package could use a bit of cleanup to use RegisterBlahComponents functions like the java package does, but that\u0027s a separate issue. For now, if you need to export some more apex package identifiers to move this test into java/dexpreopt_test.go then I think that\u0027d be preferable to having the test here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4176,
