    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "74fc9472_f2c32048",
        "filename": "apex/apex_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 4177,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-06T16:09:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see. How tedious. This would need a rethink on how test initialisation is done - it ought to use the same registration mechanism that sets up the real thing.\n\nAs we discussed in IM, you\u0027ve added comments to getBootImageJar and buildBootImage that their tests are located here, to make them somewhat more discoverable.",
      "parentUuid": "b081f00e_bbe80f23",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4176,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4177,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "93a69e5f370619904b5473b7f224f5816d59da61",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "55ee99fa_6961a30b",
        "filename": "apex/apex_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 4177,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-06T16:54:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e  - it ought to use the same registration mechanism that sets up the real thing.\n\u003e \n\nYou can do that to some extent by following the pattern used for other methods in this code. e.g. java.RegisterAppBuildComponents(ctx).\n\nfunc init() {\n\tRegisterApexBuildComponents(android.InitRegistrationContext)\n}\n\nfunc RegisterApexBuildComponents(ctx RegistrationContext) {\n\tctx.RegisterModuleType(\"apex\", BundleFactory)\n\tctx.RegisterModuleType(\"apex_key\", ApexKeyFactory)\n\t...\n}\n\nThat at least avoids having to duplicate the registration code.\n\nAs to the import order there is nothing much you can do about that. Cycles between packages are not allowed.\n\nIf you do refactor the APEX registration code as suggested above I would recommend doing that as a separate change.",
      "parentUuid": "74fc9472_f2c32048",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4176,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4177,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "93a69e5f370619904b5473b7f224f5816d59da61",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6dbb16a6_fa84146e",
        "filename": "apex/apex_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 4177,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-06T17:11:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e As to the import order there is nothing much you can do about that.\n\nThat\u0027s why I mentioned the registration mechanism used in real runs, which after all avoids import cycles. To be useful for tests it\u0027d need an extension so that tests can enable registrations only in the packages they need in the test configs. If we had that we wouldn\u0027t need the RegisterBlahComponents functions - the init() code would do it.\n\nAnyway, that\u0027s a whole different matter from this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "55ee99fa_6961a30b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4176,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4177,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "93a69e5f370619904b5473b7f224f5816d59da61",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cc098649_0b385b63",
        "filename": "apex/apex_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 4177,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-07T15:27:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The calling of the init() functions and the import cycle checking is a fundamental part of go and is cooked into it from the compiler to the runtime. If package X depends on package Y and Z then all the init() functions in package Y and Z are run before the init() function in X, well before any tests have been run.",
      "parentUuid": "6dbb16a6_fa84146e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4176,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 4177,
        "endChar": 51
      },
